1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,779
Hello!

2
00:00:00,779 --> 00:00:07,483
This week you will learn the structure of the IELTS exam, the four marking criteria,

3
00:00:07,483 --> 00:00:09,957
and three basic grammar points:

4
00:00:09,957 --> 00:00:13,548
tenses, articles, and subject-verb agreement.

5
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,546
The Academic test has four skills.

6
00:00:17,546 --> 00:00:21,117
Listening has four parts and forty questions.

7
00:00:21,117 --> 00:00:24,609
Reading has three passages in sixty minutes.

8
00:00:24,609 --> 00:00:30,085
Writing has two tasks, and Task 2 counts double compared with Task 1.

9
00:00:30,085 --> 00:00:32,069
Speaking has three parts.

10
00:00:32,069 --> 00:00:38,656
This is our own summary, so please check the official website before your test day.

11
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:43,604
Listening, Reading, Writing, Speaking.

12
00:00:45,904 --> 00:00:50,181
Writing and Speaking are each marked on four criteria.

13
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:51,131
For Writing:

14
00:00:51,131 --> 00:00:55,566
task response, coherence and cohesion, lexical resource,

15
00:00:55,566 --> 00:00:58,338
and grammatical range and accuracy.

16
00:00:58,338 --> 00:00:59,368
For Speaking:

17
00:00:59,368 --> 00:01:05,070
fluency and coherence, lexical resource, grammatical range and accuracy,

18
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:06,496
and pronunciation.

19
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:09,365
Task Response.

20
00:01:09,365 --> 00:01:11,944
Coherence and Cohesion.

21
00:01:11,944 --> 00:01:13,849
Lexical Resource.

22
00:01:13,849 --> 00:01:17,324
Grammatical Range and Accuracy.

23
00:01:20,624 --> 00:01:22,031
Grammar point one:

24
00:01:22,031 --> 00:01:22,578
tenses.

25
00:01:22,578 --> 00:01:29,301
The present perfect connects the past with the present, and it goes with for or since.

26
00:01:29,301 --> 00:01:34,616
A finished time, like yesterday or last year, needs the past simple.

27
00:01:35,916 --> 00:01:39,032
I have lived in Da Nang for five years.

28
00:01:39,032 --> 00:01:41,748
I moved here in twenty twenty-one.

29
00:01:45,048 --> 00:01:46,402
Grammar point two:

30
00:01:46,402 --> 00:01:47,079
articles.

31
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:52,343
Choose a or an by the first sound of the next word, not by the letter.

32
00:01:52,343 --> 00:01:57,984
When you talk about plural or uncountable nouns in general, use no article.

33
00:01:59,284 --> 00:02:01,755
She is an honest person.

34
00:02:01,755 --> 00:02:04,534
He studies at a university.

35
00:02:04,534 --> 00:02:07,108
Music helps people relax.

36
00:02:10,408 --> 00:02:11,858
Grammar point three:

37
00:02:11,858 --> 00:02:13,524
subject-verb agreement.

38
00:02:13,524 --> 00:02:17,511
Find the head noun and ignore the prepositional phrase.

39
00:02:17,511 --> 00:02:22,294
Advice and research are uncountable, so they take a singular verb.

40
00:02:22,294 --> 00:02:23,453
One easy mix-up:

41
00:02:23,453 --> 00:02:28,744
the number of takes a singular verb, but a number of takes a plural verb.

42
00:02:30,044 --> 00:02:32,035
The advice was useful.

43
00:02:32,035 --> 00:02:34,841
One of my friends lives abroad.

44
00:02:34,841 --> 00:02:37,556
A number of students are late.

45
00:02:40,856 --> 00:02:44,440
Three common mistakes for Vietnamese learners.

46
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:44,752
One:

47
00:02:44,752 --> 00:02:49,817
using the present perfect with a finished time such as yesterday.

48
00:02:49,817 --> 00:02:50,129
Two:

49
00:02:50,129 --> 00:02:53,012
leaving out the article before a job.

50
00:02:53,012 --> 00:02:53,479
Three:

51
00:02:53,479 --> 00:02:58,544
adding s to uncountable nouns, for example advice or information.

52
00:02:59,844 --> 00:03:02,133
I met him yesterday.

53
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,078
She is a teacher.

54
00:03:04,078 --> 00:03:06,252
I need some advice.

55
00:03:09,552 --> 00:03:11,539
Mini quiz, three questions.

56
00:03:11,539 --> 00:03:15,291
Listen carefully, choose your answers in your head,

57
00:03:15,291 --> 00:03:18,528
and then hear the answers in the next scene.

58
00:03:19,828 --> 00:03:20,340
One.

59
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:25,970
She has worked here blank twenty twenty-two.

60
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,761
For, or since?

61
00:03:27,761 --> 00:03:28,273
Two.

62
00:03:28,273 --> 00:03:31,599
He is blank M-B-A student.

63
00:03:31,599 --> 00:03:32,751
A, or an?

64
00:03:32,751 --> 00:03:33,519
Three.

65
00:03:33,519 --> 00:03:38,509
Mathematics blank my favourite subject.

66
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:39,916
Is, or are?

67
00:03:46,216 --> 00:03:46,879
Answers.

68
00:03:46,879 --> 00:03:47,211
One:

69
00:03:47,211 --> 00:03:51,520
since, because twenty twenty-two is a point in time.

70
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:51,851
Two:

71
00:03:51,851 --> 00:03:57,901
an, because MBA is pronounced em-bee-ay, which starts with a vowel sound.

72
00:03:57,901 --> 00:03:58,398
Three:

73
00:03:58,398 --> 00:04:03,784
is, because mathematics is uncountable and takes a singular verb.

74
00:04:06,084 --> 00:04:06,666
Summary:

75
00:04:06,666 --> 00:04:13,066
you now know the exam format, the four marking criteria, and three basic grammar points.

76
00:04:13,066 --> 00:04:18,594
Next, do the thirty practice questions in the app, then take the entry test.

77
00:04:18,594 --> 00:04:20,922
There is no pass mark this week.

78
00:04:20,922 --> 00:04:24,631
Just record your score and your first ten mistakes,

79
00:04:24,631 --> 00:04:27,540
so you can compare them with week eight.
